Z||000000||batboy||08-14-99||12:13 PM||||I mail ordered an in-dash Auto Meter Sport-Comp series speedometer and tachometer from JEGS. When I looked at the instructions for the speedo, the wiring diagram did not match. Much annoyed, I called the Auto Meter customer service phone number. No waiting! A human being answered right away. I told them the problem. They replied that they were now aware of that problem and had fixed it by putting different instructions in the boxes being shipped now. He then offered to mail the correct instructions out or fax them. Ten minutes later, I had a faxed set in my hands. <br>Later on, I discovered that in order to fit the tach into the instrument cluster, I had to remove the light bulb socket because it stuck out the back too far. I looked in a bunch of auto parts and hardware stores with no luck. I emailed Auto Meter in desperation. The next day I got a nice reply back from them saying that they had a special flush mount bulb socket to fit that tach and they were immediately sending it out via U.S. snail mail and free of charge. I received it about three days later and it works perfect.<p>I just wanted to give Auto Meter Products Inc. some recognition for good customer service and for assisting me in completing a difficult modification task. Not many companies nowadays would send an accessory for their product to a customer for free. I'll probably buy a set of their gauges for my 1950 Chevy truck too.
